  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-13), on the browser build published with v0.19.0 (`/app/` on the Pages site).\n\nWhat happens: in the wasm build, the file commands do not work: opening a model, Open (project), Save and Save As. No dialog appears and nothing is opened or written. The maintainer expects every other system dialog to fail the same way (export G-code / post output, import and export of tool libraries, machine files, any folder or file picker).\n\nExpected: each file command works in the browser, or is visibly disabled with a reason. A command that silently does nothing is the wrong outcome.\n\nEvidence and context:\n- The pickers on wasm32 answer \"cancelled\" (stated in draft PR #1314, part of #31, which adds an async picker for opening a model or a project only).\n- The v0.19.0 release notes list \"the file picker is still owed\" as a known issue; this issue is the tracked item for it.\n- Save, Save As and every export are not covered by #1314: the browser needs a download (or the File System Access API where present) instead of a native save dialog.\n\nTo do:\n1. List every call site of a native file or folder dialog in `crates/ui` and `crates/app`, and say for each what the browser build does today.\n2. Open paths: land or finish #1314's async picker.\n3. Save paths (project save, save as, posted program, exports): write through a browser download, through the same commands the desktop build uses.\n4. Until a path works, its menu item and button are disabled on wasm with a tooltip saying why.\n\nDone means: on the browser build a model and a project can be opened, a project can be saved and saved under a new name, and a posted program can be downloaded; every other file command either works or is disabled with a reason; the structural UI tests pin the disabled state for the wasm target where they can; the release notes' known issue is removed.\n\nPart of #31. Related: PR #1314.\n",
